WEBVTT

00:01.170 --> 00:02.350
Elias.

00:04.160 --> 00:10.330
When we first met, why did you say
 you intended to make me your bride?

00:14.860 --> 00:16.090
Well...

00:19.890 --> 00:22.230
Tell me later, okay?

00:41.680 --> 00:43.220
Renfred.

00:45.020 --> 00:45.880
What?

00:46.650 --> 00:52.910
Have you ever considered taking
 someone as your spouse?

00:53.460 --> 00:54.660
Huh?

02:31.390 --> 02:35.020
I'm looking for examples
I might use to explain.

02:35.540 --> 02:36.710
Ah, to <i>her</i>, huh?

02:37.660 --> 02:40.020
What about your girl?

02:40.020 --> 02:41.260
What about her?

02:41.700 --> 02:47.190
Alice has a lot of magic power, but she 
doesn't quite have the talent to match.

02:48.380 --> 02:53.390
I thought you were bringing her 
up to maintain your lineage.

02:55.430 --> 03:00.270
I'll admit that a lot of 
sorcerers think that way.

03:02.490 --> 03:04.990
But she's my daughter!

03:06.140 --> 03:08.020
I took her in!

03:08.020 --> 03:09.530
She's a slow learner.

03:09.530 --> 03:10.960
She's not physically tough.

03:11.280 --> 03:15.100
She's stubborn and clumsy, but she's honest.

03:15.690 --> 03:18.370
She's become attached to 
a combative guy like me.

03:19.220 --> 03:21.310
Unlike me, she smiles a lot.

03:22.000 --> 03:25.220
I would never have raised her 
for such a senseless reason.

03:25.740 --> 03:27.620
I'll protect her.

03:28.120 --> 03:31.800
Until she can make her own 
decisions and live her own life.

03:32.230 --> 03:34.020
That's my duty.

04:07.190 --> 04:08.200
Alice.

04:08.200 --> 04:10.250
Sorry to call you out of the blue.

04:10.250 --> 04:12.380
And for making you pick me up, too.

04:12.380 --> 04:13.420
It's fine.

04:13.420 --> 04:15.580
There aren't any buses this late.

04:16.890 --> 04:19.120
Hi, nice to meet you.

04:19.120 --> 04:20.760
Call me Simon.

04:20.760 --> 04:21.940
I'm Alice.

04:21.940 --> 04:24.160
Nice to meet you, um...

04:24.720 --> 04:27.250
He's a priest who's familiar
with our circumstances.

04:27.650 --> 04:29.290
Okay, let's go.

04:33.470 --> 04:37.210
I never would have thought you'd come 
to me about something like this.

04:37.820 --> 04:42.080
I'm sorry, I just couldn't 
think of anyone else to ask.

04:42.080 --> 04:43.270
That's all right.

04:43.730 --> 04:47.510
I'm really glad you made a friend, though.

04:48.190 --> 04:53.870
N-Not really <i>friends</i>, so much as 
someone in the same situation.

04:55.200 --> 04:56.840
Did you know?

04:56.840 --> 05:01.230
You can describe a fact 
using many different words.

05:01.230 --> 05:05.630
And you can summarize many different 
facts using just one word.

05:06.110 --> 05:07.110
Uh-huh...

05:07.560 --> 05:11.400
How many copies of the Bible do you 
think there are throughout the world?

05:11.400 --> 05:13.120
Th-The Bible?

05:14.450 --> 05:17.830
Over three billion, according to some counts.

05:17.830 --> 05:19.860
That figure is contested, though.

05:19.860 --> 05:21.200
That's a lot.

05:21.640 --> 05:26.280
Do you think everyone who's read 
it interprets it the same way?

05:26.660 --> 05:27.620
No.

05:27.850 --> 05:28.800
Exactly.

05:28.800 --> 05:34.630
The same words and bits of information 
mean something different to each person.

05:35.670 --> 05:37.020
Right...

05:37.020 --> 05:38.250
You asked for her help,

05:38.250 --> 05:41.110
and she spent three hours of 
her time to pick you up.

05:41.110 --> 05:45.630
And she, despite not liking to ask for 
help, was kind enough to rely on me.

05:46.740 --> 05:52.770
So, I took the liberty of assuming that 
the two of you are close friends.

05:53.280 --> 05:54.580
My apologies.

05:56.510 --> 05:58.510
No, well...

05:58.950 --> 06:00.550
We <i>are</i> friends.

06:01.740 --> 06:02.960
I appreciate the honesty!

06:06.830 --> 06:08.340
Here we are.

06:14.180 --> 06:15.920
Thank you.

06:16.180 --> 06:18.570
I'd like to repay you later.

06:18.570 --> 06:20.140
Thank you.

06:20.140 --> 06:21.180
Don't worry about it.

06:21.180 --> 06:22.010
Good night.

06:22.380 --> 06:23.850
Good night.

06:31.740 --> 06:32.940
What is this?

06:32.940 --> 06:34.140
What's it called?

06:34.140 --> 06:36.260
It's different somehow.

06:36.260 --> 06:37.040
Do you like it?

06:37.380 --> 06:38.400
It's great.

06:38.400 --> 06:39.710
I want the recipe.

06:40.600 --> 06:43.740
What brings you here without Renfred?

06:44.370 --> 06:47.640
I'm borrowing your apprentice for a night.

06:49.720 --> 06:51.860
I'd rather not lend her out.

06:51.860 --> 06:53.510
You've got Ruth.

06:53.510 --> 06:54.720
Ew.

06:54.720 --> 06:56.360
That's my line.

06:56.930 --> 07:00.840
Elias, I'll sleep in your room tomorrow.

07:03.810 --> 07:05.440
Oh, fine.

07:05.440 --> 07:08.200
Are you two sleeping together?

07:29.150 --> 07:30.650
Did something happen?

07:36.470 --> 07:40.710
Have you ever experienced
 suddenly being told

07:40.710 --> 07:44.730
you don't need to do something that 
you were determined to pull off?

07:45.630 --> 07:50.570
I'm still in the middle of studying and 
training, but I thought I could do it.

07:51.170 --> 07:55.990
But it turns out that I wasn't 
being useful to Master at all.

07:58.300 --> 08:00.860
How could I forget?

08:01.920 --> 08:04.090
The same thing happened way back when, too.

08:07.510 --> 08:11.970
It was like fireworks on 
New Years or Guy Fawkes Night.

08:13.000 --> 08:17.870
The scene was just as vibrant 
and just as wretched.

08:19.660 --> 08:22.180
Master, want some coffee?

08:22.440 --> 08:23.780
The powdered stuff you bought in bulk?

08:23.780 --> 08:27.150
Crap, I was supposed to open 
the stuff he gave me first.

08:29.550 --> 08:31.980
Were we expecting someone?

08:31.980 --> 08:32.850
No.

08:35.020 --> 08:36.190
A kid?

08:37.020 --> 08:38.120
I'll get it.

08:38.560 --> 08:39.540
Be careful.

08:40.810 --> 08:41.590
Right.

08:43.730 --> 08:45.590
Hello, Miss.

08:46.140 --> 08:47.710
Who the hell are you?

08:48.540 --> 08:50.540
Are you his apprentice?

08:50.540 --> 08:51.780
You don't look like him.

08:51.780 --> 08:53.140
So not his daughter, either.

08:54.270 --> 08:55.870
Did someone send you?

08:55.870 --> 08:59.150
Oh, sorry, I haven't even introduced myself.

09:00.020 --> 09:01.760
I'm Joseph.

09:02.100 --> 09:05.850
Some seeds I sowed a long time ago 
ended up producing a good yield.

09:06.200 --> 09:08.760
So I'd like your cooperation.

09:08.760 --> 09:09.970
Huh?

09:09.970 --> 09:13.060
What the hell are you going on about?!

09:27.500 --> 09:29.870
It's just like I heard.

09:29.870 --> 09:31.710
You protect your bodyguard.

09:30.430 --> 09:31.710
Master...

09:33.250 --> 09:34.170
Master!

09:34.170 --> 09:36.060
You're too soft.

09:36.060 --> 09:37.250
You...

09:47.220 --> 09:49.320
You're not strong enough for me.

09:51.830 --> 09:57.680
You shouldn't expose your 
weakness like that, Mikhail Renfred.

09:58.830 --> 10:00.950
<i>Weakness...</i>

10:01.270 --> 10:06.830
You seemed the most cooperative. 
Guess I was right.

10:07.290 --> 10:10.500
You're going to die if you 
don't do something about that.

10:10.500 --> 10:13.010
I'll stop the pain and bleeding for you.

10:13.010 --> 10:15.710
Oh, you're doing it yourself.

10:19.950 --> 10:21.470
What do you want?

10:21.810 --> 10:26.940
First off, I want to claim the 
corruption in the Kingdom of Cats.

10:27.810 --> 10:29.560
The corruption?

10:29.830 --> 10:34.020
It's gonna make a good ingredient 
in something I'm making.

10:35.430 --> 10:38.890
You don't have very long 
hair for a sorcerer.

10:39.470 --> 10:41.950
Do you specialize in logical construction?

10:42.650 --> 10:44.240
Well, anyway...

10:47.380 --> 10:49.530
I'd rather you don't have magic power.

10:49.530 --> 10:52.090
I can't have you resisting, after all.

10:52.310 --> 10:55.550
I'll redraw these for you, too.

10:56.200 --> 11:00.420
That way, you'll remember you've got a chain 
around your neck every time you look in the mirror.

11:02.890 --> 11:04.070
I like it.

11:05.060 --> 11:08.980
Well, I should probably explain.

11:09.610 --> 11:14.660
Don't worry, I'll give you your 
arm back as soon as I'm done.

11:18.070 --> 11:22.180
I was so preoccupied with what
 was happening at the time.

11:22.650 --> 11:25.110
Master protected me.

11:25.730 --> 11:28.730
And we couldn't even get his arm back.

11:28.730 --> 11:31.730
I've grown taller, but I'm not any stronger.

11:32.080 --> 11:35.140
And yet here I am, acting like 
some badass bodyguard.

11:38.690 --> 11:41.250
He said I'm a daughter to him.

11:43.650 --> 11:45.610
"Daughter"?! What the shit?!

11:45.610 --> 11:49.880
Thanks for raising your
 "bodyguard," damn it!

11:50.260 --> 11:53.390
Sure, it was my own decision, but...

11:54.370 --> 11:57.070
And it made you sad to hear him say that?

12:00.060 --> 12:01.910
I didn't hate it, I guess.

12:02.790 --> 12:05.930
I've lived with him at his
 house this whole time.

12:09.090 --> 12:11.420
Like you would with your family.

12:11.940 --> 12:14.160
But it still sucked to hear it.

12:16.740 --> 12:20.680
I don't think of Master as my dad.

12:20.680 --> 12:25.930
My idea of a father is 
a pathetic, worthless junkie.

12:28.390 --> 12:30.880
Not someone as awesome as he is.

12:32.040 --> 12:33.540
That's complicated.

12:39.910 --> 12:41.790
What about you?

12:41.790 --> 12:42.830
Me?

12:43.190 --> 12:45.310
You're sleeping with him.

12:45.310 --> 12:47.610
You aren't just master 
and apprentice, are you?

12:49.970 --> 12:51.740
I guess not.

12:52.700 --> 12:55.200
I don't really know, either.

12:55.980 --> 12:58.860
He's my master, technically.

12:58.860 --> 13:03.550
But we're technically also married, so...

13:03.550 --> 13:04.820
Married...

13:04.820 --> 13:06.120
You're in pretty deep.

13:06.120 --> 13:08.190
I don't really think about it, usually.

13:08.190 --> 13:11.260
Maybe we are, maybe we aren't.

13:12.210 --> 13:16.510
I think other people usually use 
a different word to describe it.

13:17.560 --> 13:22.560
That thing Simon said about people 
having different interpretations?

13:24.050 --> 13:25.180
Yeah.

13:26.520 --> 13:31.240
But whatever we call it, it doesn't 
change what it really is.

13:32.440 --> 13:37.330
There are different ways of thinking 
about it, but the truth is still the same.

13:37.960 --> 13:40.790
Renfred-san has his own interpretation

13:40.790 --> 13:44.750
of your relationship with him, 
and you have your own, too.

13:45.650 --> 13:48.210
Maybe it's the same thing 
with a different name.

13:50.270 --> 13:55.820
Still, though, how would you feel 
if someone said Elias is your dad?

13:59.320 --> 14:01.050
You're so silly.

14:01.050 --> 14:02.280
Brother.

14:02.280 --> 14:05.320
Who even cares what he thinks?

14:05.620 --> 14:09.180
You want to become his bodyguard, don't you?

14:09.180 --> 14:12.780
If you don't intend to change that,
 what's there to worry about?

14:13.080 --> 14:15.220
Like I <i>said</i>...

14:17.090 --> 14:20.120
I mean, yeah, you're right! But...

14:21.630 --> 14:23.410
I...

14:27.410 --> 14:28.640
You're what?

14:29.200 --> 14:30.270
I'm sleeping!

14:39.270 --> 14:40.500
Good night.

15:11.370 --> 15:13.770
You still aren't asleep.

15:14.390 --> 15:15.470
Nor are you.

15:15.970 --> 15:20.130
I was hearing Alice out, 
and now I can't sleep.

15:20.130 --> 15:21.840
Did she want to discuss something with you?

15:21.840 --> 15:22.640
Yes.

15:29.950 --> 15:32.120
May I ask your answer to my 
question from this morning?

15:34.500 --> 15:37.820
Can I think about it a bit longer?

15:37.820 --> 15:40.780
There's so much to think about every day.

15:40.780 --> 15:43.330
I might forget if I wait too long.

15:51.240 --> 15:53.540
I thought it would be a convenient solution.

15:54.600 --> 15:58.430
Whether you're a spouse or an 
apprentice, you'd be living with me.

15:58.990 --> 16:04.190
If I had the same person be both, 
I'd have one less thing to deal with.

16:05.820 --> 16:07.190
Are you disappointed in me?

16:10.560 --> 16:13.730
To be honest, I expected as much.

16:13.730 --> 16:15.310
You did...

16:15.310 --> 16:16.700
I mean...

16:18.760 --> 16:19.630
Although...

16:20.850 --> 16:23.990
An apprentice eventually 
leaves their master.

16:24.980 --> 16:30.280
You became my master and
 taught me all kinds of things.

16:30.280 --> 16:31.500
You left me at one point.

16:32.240 --> 16:34.770
And then you came back.

16:35.970 --> 16:37.620
And I couldn't let you go.

16:38.170 --> 16:39.260
And...

16:40.450 --> 16:44.870
You said it was because you're my bride.

16:46.700 --> 16:49.630
A married couple is supposed 
to stick together, right?

16:50.400 --> 16:53.270
Honestly, it's not like that anymore.

16:53.630 --> 16:54.300
Eh?

16:54.780 --> 16:58.220
A lot of couples get divorced these days.

16:59.640 --> 17:03.210
I think a married couple, 
or a master and apprentice...

17:03.990 --> 17:05.700
are each just one interpretation. One role.

17:06.600 --> 17:07.620
Role?

17:08.490 --> 17:11.410
Whether you're parent and child or friends,

17:11.410 --> 17:14.220
people have all kinds of 
relationships and roles.

17:14.740 --> 17:20.640
They either take on those roles 
or wish the other person would.

17:21.450 --> 17:26.470
Depending on who you ask, people have 
different names for the same role.

17:26.990 --> 17:32.490
So we take on the roles of "master and 
apprentice" and "married couple," but...

17:33.020 --> 17:37.420
But I guess we don't have to really 
stick to those roles so strictly.

17:41.830 --> 17:47.920
Do you mean you don't appreciate being 
assigned the role of my bride or my master?

17:48.240 --> 17:50.510
No, actually, I do appreciate it.

17:50.510 --> 17:52.170
I don't hate it at all.

17:53.530 --> 17:54.690
It's just that...

17:59.760 --> 18:01.920
It doesn't matter how it started.

18:04.240 --> 18:06.100
Whatever our roles,

18:06.690 --> 18:09.940
I'm happy when I'm with you.

18:11.100 --> 18:17.580
And it makes me happy to know
 that you can't let me go.

18:27.760 --> 18:29.090
Happy?

18:31.470 --> 18:33.850
"Happy" means...

18:34.940 --> 18:38.330
I can make it through another day tomorrow.

18:38.830 --> 18:43.440
As long as I have this memory, I can 
make through a hardship or two.

18:43.440 --> 18:45.060
It cheers me up.

18:45.360 --> 18:47.420
It makes my insides go "wahhh"...

18:53.960 --> 18:55.390
I see.

18:55.390 --> 18:58.770
So, right now, I'm happy that 
I got to speak with you,

18:58.770 --> 19:01.460
and I feel lonely about 
having to go back to bed.

19:04.170 --> 19:10.450
I think I'm probably happy to take 
on the role of your husband.

19:11.390 --> 19:14.280
Is it all right if I continue in this role?

19:15.380 --> 19:19.460
Frankly, I don't know what 
I'd do if you said no.

19:25.540 --> 19:28.970
I'm still your master, too, though.

19:29.500 --> 19:30.290
Yes.

19:38.520 --> 19:43.560
<i>I never managed to figure anything out.</i>

19:44.180 --> 19:47.270
<i>And I ended up dumping all of it on Chise.</i>

19:48.040 --> 19:49.320
It's noon.

19:49.720 --> 19:50.950
What happened to class?

19:51.570 --> 19:53.140
Good morning, sir!

19:53.680 --> 19:54.630
Morning.

19:58.960 --> 20:00.800
Damn it, screw this!

20:01.360 --> 20:05.050
You might think of me as your daughter,

20:05.350 --> 20:09.050
but I don't think of you as my dad at all!

20:10.060 --> 20:11.010
What are you...

20:11.010 --> 20:14.260
I don't hate that you think 
of me as your daughter.

20:14.260 --> 20:17.430
But that's not the role I want.

20:17.430 --> 20:20.030
You keep talking about me being 
your duty or job and shit...

20:20.030 --> 20:22.750
Do you think you're inferior 
to me or something?

20:26.430 --> 20:28.940
I was the one who set you on your path.

20:29.290 --> 20:32.870
I forced it on you in a way
 you wouldn't notice.

20:32.870 --> 20:33.550
No!

20:34.090 --> 20:36.520
You <i>taught</i> me my path!

20:36.520 --> 20:39.900
And I took it because 
I thought it'd be good for me!

20:40.480 --> 20:45.310
If I hadn't taken you in, you would
 have chosen a more normal path.

20:46.410 --> 20:48.850
There are no "what ifs"!

20:49.260 --> 20:51.630
You chose <i>me</i> back then!

20:52.230 --> 20:56.180
So now it's my turn to choose <i>you</i>!

20:56.710 --> 20:59.440
Mikhail Renfred!

21:09.100 --> 21:11.670
I'm done just being protected.

21:12.660 --> 21:18.810
I'm begging you, let me protect you 
at least for that arm's worth.

21:19.720 --> 21:21.600
I'll work harder.

21:30.920 --> 21:35.990
You're still a child, so long as 
you're just standing there shouting.

21:41.620 --> 21:44.230
It's an adult's duty to protect children.

21:44.630 --> 21:48.440
If you want to protect me, you 
can start by not skipping class.

21:52.730 --> 21:55.230
You don't get it!
